+    // 1.1.3 (issue #3): takes the leading NAME=value words (NAME of capitals, digits and _, not starting with a digit)
+    // out of the command line and returns them, in order, to be set as variables; it also drops a literal "%command%".
+    // Launchers without Steam's "VAR=value %command%" pass those words as arguments, which the game took for its ELF.
+    // Only before the first other word, as in a shell: a flag's value ("--clave Clave=...") and paths stay.
